Original commit body from 375b56ce64c3d8ba0ae87c31b6f4d28fa5e4da6c:

WI-kadop proposed splitting a Symbol.synthesis_mechanism field off Symbol.origin
(mirroring ADR-0031/0032) because origin carried values naming HOW a symbol was
synthesized (inheritance / orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis /
boundary_external_symbol_synthesis / scip) rather than WHICH registered pass.

Re-verifying the premise showed the ground truth shifted: the intervening
synthetic:F1 work gave the two high-volume synthesizers (1620 + 518 self-corpus
symbols) real AnalysisRuns whose pass_id IS the origin value, with the nodes'
origin_run_id joining to it — so a synthesized symbol's "how" IS "which pass".
A field-split would then store the same string in two fields (a new redundancy),
not remove a leak. Of the other two values, `inheritance` is a phantom (zero
producers; the inheritance-linker stamps make_pass_id("inheritance-linker"),
not the bare string) and `scip` is off-self-corpus.

ADR-0044 decision: no new field. catalog._SYNTHESIS_MECHANISMS renamed
_SYNTHETIC_PASS_IDS and re-documented as legitimate synthetic pass-ids; the
`inheritance` phantom dropped; the SCIP-symbol AnalysisRun-join gap split to
WI-zabus (cross-package, rust-analyzer). No IR shape change, no SCHEMA_VERSION
bump. Precedent: a filed field-split can be correctly WITHDRAWN when intervening
work resolves the axis conflation it targeted — verify the premise before
applying a campaign pattern mechanically.

Completes WI-kadop (re-scoped; tracker status set post-merge).

